        "title": "Future Exploration: Moon, Mars, and Beyond",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The next phase of space exploration is defined by three overlapping programs: (1) Artemis — NASA's return to the Moon with international and commercial partners; (2) Mars — robotic precursors leading to eventual human missions; (3) Deep space — outer solar system science missions and the long-horizon vision of human expansion. The critical constraint on all of them is the same: launch cost, in-space propulsion capability, and life support for long-duration human missions."
